  "question": {
    "text": "With two forces acting at a point, the maximum effect is obtained when their resultant is $4 \\mathrm{~N}$. If they act at right angles, then their resultant is $3 \\mathrm{~N}$. Then the forces are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pf6Pu",
      "text": "\n$(2+\\sqrt{2}) N$ and $(2-\\sqrt{2}) N$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "W5Z8I",
      "text": "\n$(2+\\sqrt{3}) \\mathrm{N}$ and $(2-\\sqrt{3}) \\mathrm{N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "eJRnI",
      "text": "\n$\\left(2+\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{2}\\right) \\mathrm{N}$ and $\\left(2-\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{2}\\right) \\mathrm{N}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "baRmi",
      "text": "\n$\\left(2+\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{3}\\right) \\mathrm{N}$ and $\\left(2-\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{3}\\right) \\mathrm{N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P+Q=4, P^2+Q^2=9 \\Rightarrow P=\\left(2+\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{2}\\right) N$ and $Q=\\left(2-\\frac{1}{2} \\sqrt{2}\\right) N$",
    "image": null
  },
